From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ae-automation-bot <ae-automation-bot@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 11:10:34 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 289/333] [ae-patch] Fix the review findings on the
 scheduled-task account pin

Three reviewers (Sonnet, Opus security, Codex) found:
- A PATCH that set claude_account with a host_id asked that host which
  accounts it holds before the ownership check, so another user's host could
  be probed. The pin is now checked after the host's ownership check.
- A pin outlived a move to a managed sandbox, to another agent or to another
  host. It is now dropped on a sandbox or agent switch unless the request
  sets one, and re-checked against the new host; a sandbox task cannot be
  pinned.
- A task on a Claude SDK or other non-Claude-Code agent could be pinned, but
  only claude-native reads the label, so it ran on the active account. A pin
  now needs a claude-native agent.
- shared: plus a 64-character name is 71 characters; the limit and column
  are now 80.
- The update tool schema now allows null, the only way to clear a pin.
- The form showed a blank trigger for a default-login pin the host does not
  list; a create that cannot store its pin now deletes the task.
